<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Manifest for northwind-sales step M3-S05.

  Two types, and the pairing is the point: skills/admin/lightning-record-page-configuration
  SKILL.md "Pattern: Moving a Page and Its Assignment Between Orgs" and gotchas.md Gotcha 1
  both state that a manifest naming only FlexiPage is "incomplete by definition" - the
  CustomObject member is what carries the org default.

  CustomApplication is the third type that pattern names, and it is absent here on purpose:
  this build writes no application file, so there is no app-level override to ship. That is
  not the same as there being none in the org. See deploy-order.md section 3 and assumption
  A38 - an app with its own Opportunity record page outranks this org default and must be
  re-pointed in Setup by hand.

  Members are named explicitly rather than with *, so that the manifest and the files on disk
  agree in both directions: every file covered by a member, every member backed by a file.
  That is what the step's manifest acceptance test asserts.

  Version 62.0. The step's inputs{} carry no api_version and plan.json carries no top-level
  api_version key, so agents/metadata-builder/AGENT.md Inputs resolves it to the documented
  62.0 default. It also matches every other package.xml under artefacts/ in this build.
-->
<Package xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <types>
        <members>Opportunity_Enterprise_Record_Page</members>
        <name>FlexiPage</name>
    </types>
    <types>
        <members>Opportunity</members>
        <name>CustomObject</name>
    </types>
    <version>62.0</version>
</Package>
